 * its sources were opened on 1 Nov 2026 and the page amended where a source
 * said less (research/waiting-for-the-tie-in/VERDICTS.md); what would not
 * open is marked as reported or waits on the owner.
 *
 * The web edition has three scripted pieces, and none of their script ships,
 * because the whole site's client budget is 6 kB and the originals are 13.
 * Each is computed here at build from the web edition's own data, copied
 * below as it stands, and set as static figures:
 *   03 · the chain: 21 cards in the edition's order, each with what the piece
 *        needs, what it enables, its years to replace, its critical path from
 *        a standing start and what becomes impossible downstream without it,
 *        by the same two functions the explorer ran on a click (`path`,
 *        `dead`).
 *   05 · the model: every input with its published default and the note its
 *        slider carried, then the model run once at those defaults by the
 *        explorer's own `sim`: the readout, what binds each year, two bar
 *        figures and the year table.
 *   08 · side by side: the four tabs as four tables, every row with its note;
 *        a row's source is its number in section 12 where the list carries
 *        the row's address, else the address printed as text.
 * The two sentences in 03 and the two in 05 and 12 that told a reader to
 * select, remove, try or move something now say what the static figure shows.
 * One word is changed three times: "leading" (a chain piece's title, a row of
 * section 08 and its prose, "its leading node") reads "most advanced",
 * because tools/check-brand.cjs bans the word and cannot tell a description
 * from praise, as Edition 01's "curated" became "selected".
 */
