      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="02" title="Sold out<br>to 2031." id="machines">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono-b">02 · The machines</p>
        <p>Suppose the grid said yes tomorrow. The power still has to come from somewhere, and firm power in America means gas turbines.</p>
        <p>Three companies are the main makers of the large ones. <span class="cite">{c(10)}</span> GE Vernova's backlog and slot reservations reached 116 gigawatts by the end of June, and it is now taking reservations for 2031 delivery. <span class="cite">{c(9, 109)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> Siemens Energy holds 69 gigawatts in backlog, and its finance chief puts lead times across the company at three years or more. <span class="cite">{c(110, 11)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> Mitsubishi Power's large-frame backlog is 35 gigawatts, up from 23 a year earlier. <span class="cite">{c(111, 12)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> Wood Mackenzie counted about 110 gigawatts on order at the end of 2025 against 60 to 70 gigawatts of global manufacturing capacity, with prices expected to reach roughly 195 percent above 2019 by the end of 2027. <span class="cite">{c(13)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span></p>
        <p>The summary said the turbines come from China. They don't. In the reporting we cite, to July 2026, no Chinese large-frame turbine had been delivered to the United States; the first North American order, for Canada, came in March 2026. <span class="cite">{c(14, 59)}</span> Dongfang's first self-developed F-class export, its 50 megawatt G50, was shipped to Kazakhstan in late 2025. <span class="cite">{c(14, 59)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> The bottleneck is in South Carolina, Berlin and Takasago, and those factories are sold out.</p>
        <p>Then the transformer. Every plant and every data centre needs one to step voltage up or down. A large power transformer took about 128 weeks to arrive in mid 2025 and a generator step-up unit about 144, and power transformer prices are up 77 percent since 2019. <span class="cite">{c(15)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> One American company, Cleveland-Cliffs by its own account, makes grain-oriented electrical steel, the steel inside them. <span class="cite">{c(112, 16)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span> China holds about 60 percent of the world's capacity to make transformers, <span class="cite">{c(17)}</span> and since 26 August 2026 an executive order lets the Energy Secretary bar new transactions in bulk-power equipment from China and other covered countries on the US grid. <span class="cite">{c(115, 116, 18)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.F}>F</span></p>
        <p class="beat">An order placed today for the machine that makes the power arrives around 2030 or later at GE Vernova; Mitsubishi's latest orders are scheduled for 2028 to 2030. <span class="cite">{c(109, 12)}</span> <span class="mark" aria-label={MARK.I}>I</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-b side">
        <figure class="field bars" aria-label="Gas turbine backlogs by manufacturer">
